 "text": "Metro\nSkip to main content\ncollapse all\nEvents\nNews and stories\nTools and data\nContact\nLanguage hub\nWhat Metro does\nWhat Metro does\nProjects\nConnecting regional priorities\nGarbage and recycling system\nHousing and homelessness\nLand use and development\nParks and nature investments\nTransportation\nTools and data\nVisitor venues\nGet involved\nGet involved\nGive your input\nCommittees\nFind funding\nPublic engagement\nWaste disposal and prevention\nWaste disposal and prevention\nNeed to get rid of something?\nHealthy living and waste reduction\nReport dumped garbage\nEducation resources\nParks and nature\nParks and nature\nParks\nBoat ramps\nCemeteries\nGuided nature activities\nReservations and services\nSafety and policies\nAbout Metro\nAbout Metro\nMetro Council\nMetro Auditor\nMERC\nStructure and operations\nCivil rights at Metro\nMetro Code\nAccessibility at Metro\nEquity at Metro\nDoing business with Metro\nPublic records\nJobs\nEvents\nNews and stories\nTools and data\nContact\nLanguage hub\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nWelcome to Metro\nYour regional government works with communities across greater Portland to plan for the future and manage public services and systems that cross city and county lines.\nAdd your voice\nHere for you\nMetro grants\nExplore funding for projects in land, transportation, nature, and climate. Apply for open grants today.\nJobs at Metro\nWe’re hiring! Bring your skills and experience to Metro and help shape our region’s future.\nAsk an expert\nNeed help with garbage or recycling? Our experts are ready to answer—in English or Spanish.\nFuture Vision project\nMetro is bringing together communities across greater Portland to create a 50-year visionary outlook for the region.\nLearn more about Future Vision\nBlue Lake Regional Park improvements\nPeople have come to Blue Lake for generations to gather, play, and connect with nature. But the infrastructure at the park is aging, and improvements are needed to keep Blue Lake Regional Park fun, safe and welcoming.\nLearn more about park improvements\nMetro Council\nThe Metro Council consists of a president, elected regionwide, and six councilors who are elected by district every four years in nonpartisan races.\nWho is my councilor?\nMeet the council\nRegional priorities\nEnvironmental protection\nMetro prioritizes the environment and the climate in decisions about regional systems and long-range planning to protect clean air and water and preserve this region’s natural beauty for future generations.\nResilient economy\nMetro works to ensure the greater Portland region is an affordable and quality place for people and businesses.\nHousing for all\nMetro is working to create thriving communities throughout the greater Portland region where everyone has a safe, stable and affordable home.\nEvents\nSee more events\nfull\nToday\n9:30 to 11:30 a.m.\nNature activity\nMushroom hike\nIn person\nChehalem Ridge Nature Park\nToday\n10 a.m. to noon\nNature activity\nReimagining birding: waterfowl\nIn person\nHowell Territorial Park\nfull\nToday\n12:30 to 2:30 p.m.\nNature activity\nMushroom hike\nIn person\nChehalem Ridge Nature Park\nOpportunities\nGive your input\nJobs\nGrants and funding\nContracts\nServices\nAsk a garbage and recycling expert\nApply for a contractor's business license\nBuy a parks pass\nBuy a cemetery plot\nGet language assistance\nGet ADA assistance\nMetro employee hub\nPay my SHS tax\nLeadership\nMetro Council\nWho is my councilor?\nMetro Auditor\nCommittees\nWhether your roots in the region run generations deep or you moved to Oregon last week, you have your own reasons for loving this place — and Metro wants to keep it that way. Help shape the future of the greater Portland region and discover tools, services and places that make life better today.\nContact Metro\n503-797-1700\nRelay service 711\nSend a message\nOregon Convention Center\nOregon Zoo\nPortland Expo Center\nPortland'5 Centers for the Arts\nFind Metro on\n© Oregon Metro. All rights reserved.",
